/ lib/amber_ai_memory.k  -  amber-ai default memory (few-shot seed corpus).
/ .
/ Loaded READ-ONLY, into ai.SEED, beside the user's own ~/.amber_ai_memory.k
/ (which lives in ai.M). Keeping the two apart is deliberate:
/   * `\ai forget` clears what YOU taught it and leaves this intact;
/   * ai.save never writes these back into your personal memory file;
/   * ai.MAX trimming only ever evicts your records, never the corpus.
/ ai.top ranks over ai.M,ai.SEED, so your own lines are searched first and
/ win ties -- the corpus is a floor, not a ceiling.
/ .
/     ai.seed[kind;text;context]
/ .
/ EVERY expression below was executed against a gentq-generated trades/quotes
/ workspace, through the same qsql.k rewriter the REPL runs your keystrokes
/ through, and is known to evaluate without error. Regenerate and re-check
/ with tests/verify_memory.k.
/ .
/ Time bucketing is the TWO-STEP form, and that is not a style choice:
/     bars:update tb:xbar[300;time] from trades
/     select avg px by sym,tb from bars
/ "select ... by 300 xbar time from trades" PARSES and is silently WRONG --
/ the by-clause does not evaluate expressions, so the term becomes a literal
/ column name, the bucket column comes back blank and the row count equals no
/ bucketing at all. Eleven entries here taught that form until it was measured.
/ .
/ NB: the "/ ." spacer lines are not a typo. A line holding nothing but "/" opens
/ a BLOCK comment in this dialect and swallows everything to the next lone "\",
/ so a plain blank comment line here would silently disable the whole corpus --
/ and a trailing-whitespace-stripping editor would turn "/ " into exactly that.
/ .
/   qSQL           73
/   time-series    62
/   adverbs        64
/   attributes     31
/   error-fix      34
/   TOTAL          264


