/ .
/ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/ INTENT-GLOSSED EXEMPLARS (generated from data/train.jsonl)
/ .
/ The third argument is not decoration. ai.top scores a record by how many of
/ its words appear in the question, over BOTH the text and the context -- and
/ the text here is CODE, which shares a word with an English question almost
/ never. Measured over the 344 natural-language questions in data/train.jsonl,
/ text-only scoring put the right answer among the three exemplars 0 times.
/ .
/ So each line below carries the words people actually used to ask for it,
/ taken from the phrasings in the dataset rather than invented, stopwords
/ removed. That is what makes the corpus reachable.
/ .
/ Every one was executed against a gentq-generated trades/quotes workspace, and
/ that is also the filter: 64 otherwise-good expressions were dropped here
/ because they name tables a user will not have (`kt`, `v`, `w` from
/ data/fixture.k). An exemplar that references a name the reader does not have
/ teaches the name, not the idiom.
/ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/ .
ai.seed["q";"select sym,px from trades";"symbol price trades sym px trade project"]
ai.seed["q";"select sym,sz from trades";"symbol size trades sym trade every next project sz"]
ai.seed["q";"select px,sz from trades";"price size trades px sz numeric project"]
ai.seed["q";"select time,px from trades";"time price every trade trades series against project px"]
ai.seed["q";"select sym,time,px from trades";"symbol time price trades everything size project sym px"]
ai.seed["q";"select from trades";"whole trades unchanged"]
ai.seed["q";"select * from trades";"select everything trades"]
